2026-08-25T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-1036) 'Model packaging convention
 # uuid: eaf67d10-188f-5f60-a022-c26711c6973f
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:flight-level:l2, rfd:attest-in:none
 RFD:Committed  1 RFD
 Serials:Weftspun

2026-08-25T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-1036) 'model packaging
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-1036) 'Each model ships as a plain Docker image that serves HTTP, and never as a Cog package.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-1036) 'The DGX API ran each model through its own adapter, each with its own weight loader, CUDA pin, and output writer.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-1036) 'Check a new model image against the rule above before you merge it: a plain Docker image that serves HTTP, with a `Dockerfile`, a `server.py`, and a `test_input.json`.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-1036) 'Model packaging convention
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-1036) 'Package each model as a plain Docker image that serves HTTP.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-1036) 'No Cog. Cog wraps a `Predictor` class and builds an image around it, and that image expects Replicate's own runtime. The local worker starts a container and maps a port, and nothing more.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-1036) 'Each model gets a standalone repo, and each repo holds a `Dockerfile`, a `server.py`, and a `test_input.json`. The RFD stays here.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-1036) 'Name the repo for its model, and never for a package format. A format is a decision this RFD already changed once. A folder name that carries one goes stale on the next change.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-1036) 'RFD66606-1016 lists the models. RFD66606-1025 gives the memory. RFD66606-1027 the GPU tier. RFD66606-1037 the composite convention. RFD66606-1053 the asset format. RFD66606-1028 gates the license.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-1036) 'Retracted: Replicate Cog as the package format
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-1036) 'This RFD first selected Replicate Cog. Cog is a good package format, and it targets one host. RFD66606-1055 now runs the worker on this box's own 4090 first, plain Docker, no rental. vast.ai stays priced for later, the same plain-Docker shape once this box is not enough.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-1036) 'The rule that replaced it is in the README, and the reason Cog does not fit either host is beside it. This entry stays so a reader who finds a Cog reference elsewhere knows which way the decision went.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-1036) 'The target
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-1036) 'The local desktop GPU is the only compute (CLAUDE.md hard constraint). Rented GPU providers are blocklisted (RunPod, Vast.ai rows). The convention still targets a 24 GB card so an image built here runs unchanged if the operator later stands up a peer machine with equivalent hardware; RFD66606-1027 records that every model in the catalog reaches a 24 GB card.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-1036) 'An earlier draft named "RTX 4090 with 24 GB, at about 0.35 to 0.37 US dollars per hour on demand, and 0.13 interruptible" as the target and Vast.ai as a future host. Retracted: no budget for per-hour/per-invocation billing this cycle.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-1036) 'The rules
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-1036) '- One model per image. An image that holds two cannot scale one without the other.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-1036) '- Load the weights at start, and not per request. Whether the host is this box or a rented instance, a load per request buys nothing and costs every response.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-1036) '- Serve `/health` and `/predict`. Neither this box's own worker nor vast.ai runs a health probe of its own, thus a caller polls `/health` until the instance is ready.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-1036) '- Download the weights at build time. A cold start that pulls 24 GB is a cold start that times out.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-1036) '- Pin every version, and pin the upstream commit. A moved tag changes the output with no build change to show for it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-1036) '- Return 400 for a bad request, and not 500. A 500 sends a caller to retry a request that can never work.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-1036) '- Return a USD layer beside the transmission file. RFD66606-1053 gives that rule.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-1036) '- Name the license. RFD66606-1028 gates what ships.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-1036) 'Two stages in one Dockerfile
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-1036) 'The `contract` stage carries the server and `usd-core`, and no model. It builds in seconds on any machine, and `WEFTSPUN_STUB=1` makes `/predict` answer with the real shape and no GPU.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-1036) 'The `worker` stage is the real image. It carries CUDA, the upstream source, and the weights.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-1036) 'That split makes the contract testable. RFD66606-1040 records a run of it in Docker on a machine with no NVIDIA device.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-1036) 'Files in each folder
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-1036) '| File            | Holds                                       |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-1036) '| --------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-1036) '| README.md       | The RFD. Why this model, and what it costs. |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-1036) '| Dockerfile      | Both stages, the CUDA version, the weights. |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-1036) '| server.py       | `/health`, `/predict`, and the type schema. |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-1036) '| test_input.json | One request body, for the contract stage.   |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-1036) '| domain.ex       | A composite model only. See RFD66606-1037.  |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-1036) '| problem.ex      | A composite model only. See RFD66606-1037.  |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-1036) '| plan.ex         | The solved plan. The planner writes it.     |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-1036) 'What a composite model does
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-1036) 'Five models in the catalog run more than one network. RFD66606-1037 models each one as a taskweft domain, and not as a Python script. The server then calls the plan, and each step is one action.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-1036) 'The other folders are not converted yet
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-1036) 'RFD66606-1040 is the worked example. It carries a `Dockerfile`, a `server.py`, and a `test_input.json`, and RFD66606-1040 records a run of the contract stage in Docker.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-1036) 'Fourteen model folders still carry a `cog.yaml` and a `predict.py`. This folder carries a fifteenth `cog.yaml`, the template the other fourteen copied. They describe the same models, and they name a package format this RFD no longer selects.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-1036) 'The folder names no longer carry that format. Each folder is now named for its model alone.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-1036) 'Convert one when the model is next worked on, and not in a sweep. A folder converted without a build produces a `server.py` that nobody ran, which is what the Cog files already are.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-1036) 'When it was committed
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-1036) 'Committed 2026-09-02: the convention has been in force for months; CLAUDE.md closes compute (local desktop GPU only; RunPod/Vast.ai blocklisted). Earlier rental-target framing retracted in DETAILS.md.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-1036) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-08-25T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-1036) 'There is no DGX now. This RFD first selected Cog; `DETAILS.md` records why it was withdrawn.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD1036  1 LINE
 Text:Written
